The issue `proxy isatty` suggests that when `rich` attempts to check if a file stream is a TTY (using `isatty()`), it fails or behaves unexpectedly when the file stream is wrapped by a proxy (like `FileProxy` in `rich/file_proxy.py`).

I will modify `rich/file_proxy.py` to implement `isatty()` itself, delegating the check to the underlying file object if possible, or providing a safe default if the underlying object doesn't support it, to prevent `rich/console.py` from encountering exceptions or incorrect behavior when calling `isatty()` on the proxy.

In `rich/file_proxy.py`, I will add `isatty` to the `FileProxy` class.

```python
    def isatty(self) -> bool:
        return getattr(self.__file, "isatty", lambda: False)()
```
This implementation attempts to call `isatty` on the underlying file (`self.__file`). If `isatty` is not available on the underlying file, it defaults to a lambda that returns `False`, ensuring `rich/console.py` receives a boolean and doesn't raise an exception.

I will now apply the patch.

